<title>USA: Shell says Capline March nominations 993,336 bpd.</title>
<headline>Shell says Capline March nominations 993,336 bpd.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Oil Co said Monday that nominations on the Capline crude oil pipeline for March totalled 993,336 barrels per day (bpd).</p>
<p>The actual allocation on the pipeline for February was 1,036,894 bpd, compared to nominations for that month of 1,064,070 bpd.</p>
<p>The pipeline, a major artery linking the Gulf Coast and the Midwest, has a capacity to run 1.11 million bpd and is operated by Shell.</p>
<p>The 40-inch line runs from the St. James terminal in Louisiana north to the Patoka terminal in Illinois.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
